## 2. Vector & Matrix Primitives  

| Primitive | Implementation pattern | Libraries / functions | Why it’s robust | Ref / Note |
|-----------|------------------------|------------------------|-----------------|------------|
| **Cross product** | `c = a × b` returns perpendicular vector; watch sign consistency with coordinate system. | `glm::cross`, `Unity Vector3.Cross`, `FVector::CrossProduct` | Works in `float` without iterative refinement; zero for parallel inputs → guard with length test. | GLM, 2024‑07 |
| **Dot product & angle** | `float dot = a·b`; angle = `acos(clamp(dot, -1, 1))`. Clamp avoids NaN when vectors are nearly unit length. | Same as above | Guarantees correct angle for 0–π range; always re-normalize after accumulating forces. | Unity Math, 2024‑06 |
| **Vector reflection / refraction** | `r = v – 2(v·n)n` for reflection; Snell’s law with `eta` for refraction. | `glm::reflect`, `glm::refract` | Analytical – no iteration needed; GPU GLSL mirrors same code. | GLSL Spec, v4.6, 2024 |
| **Orthogonal basis (Gram–Schmidt)** | Given v₀ (dir), choose arbitrary v₁, orthonormalize to produce stable local frame. | Custom: `v1 = normalize(v1 - dot(v1,v0)*v0)` | Used for camera “look‑at”, object axes; cheaper than full QR. | Real‑Time Rendering 4e, Akenine-Möller et al. |
| **Efficient 4×4 × 4×4 multiply** | Cache 16 temp values; unroll loops if not using SIMD mat class. | GLM `operator*`, DirectX `XMMatrixMultiply` | Matches GPU’s column-major order → upload without transpose. | DirectXMath, 2024 |

