## 3. Ray Casting & Intersection  

| Method | Core idea | Typical API | Speed tier | When to use |
|--------|-----------|-------------|------------|-------------|
| **Ray–Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB)** | “Slab method” – compute per-axis tenter/texit, find overlap interval. | `Unity Bounds.Raycast`, `glm::intersectRayAABB` | O(1) | Primary broad-phase for static worlds or BVH leaves. |
| **Ray–Sphere** | Pure quadratic discriminant (`b²-4ac`). | `Unity Vector3.Distance`, custom in GLSL/HLSL | O(1) | Quick test for orbs, bounding spheres in BVH. |
| **Ray–Plane** | `t = (d - dot(N, O)) / dot(N, D)`. | `glm::intersectRayPlane` | O(1) | Used for terrain heightmaps, clipping, decals. |
| **Ray–Triangle (Möller–Trumbore)** | Uses cross products to solve barycentric coordinates without pre-computing plane. | `btCollisionWorld::rayTest` (Bullet), `RaycastChunk` in Unity’s PhysX | O(1) per triangle | Fine for mesh‐level detail, single‐ray hits, mouse picking. |
| **BVH / Octree traversal** | Build hierarchy once; traverse with AABB tests, descending only where ray hits. | NVIDIA PhysX `rtTree`, custom C++ `BVH` class | O(log n) average | Large static scenes, high‐poly meshes, LOD culling. |
| **KD‐Tree with warp traversal** | Binary space partition; GPU friendly when nodes stored in Shader Storage Buffer. | Cox 2009 paper, Vulkan ray‐traversal shader | Very fast on GPUs | For baked lighting, AO, RTX ray tracing pipelines. |

### Implementation hints (C#)  
```csharp
// Fast Möller–Trumbore on struct-of-arrays
public static bool RayTriangle(out float t,
    float3 origin, float3 dir,
    float3 v0, float3 v1, float3 v2)
{
    t = 0;
    float3 e1 = v1 - v0, e2 = v2 - v0;
    float3 pdir = math.cross(dir, e2);
    float det = math.dot(e1, pdir);
    if (math.abs(det) < 1e-6f) return false;
    float inv = 1f / det;
    float3 tov0 = origin - v0;
    float u = inv * math.dot(tov0, pdir);
    if (u < 0f || u > 1f) return false;
    float3 q = math.cross(tov0, e1) * inv;
    float v = inv * math.dot(dir, q);
    if (v < 0f || u + v > 1f) return false;
    t = inv * math.dot(e2, q);
    return t > 1e-6f;
}
```
*Compile with Unity’s burst + `math` package for SIMD (ECS) or HLSL’s `triangles` counter for RTX.*

**Sources:**  
- Möller Trumbore, “Fast, Minimum Storage Ray/Triangle Intersection”, J**Continuation**

**Sources:** – Möller Trumbore, “Fast, Minimum‑Storage Ray‑Triangle Intersection”, *Journal of Graphics Tools* 1997, updated in *Real‑Time Rendering* 4th ed. (2023) <https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-12-815856-4.00009-4>.  
– NVIDIA Ray Tracing Developer Guide, “Ray‑Triangle Intersection in CUDA”, 2024‑09 <https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/rtx-accelerated-ray-tracing/>.

