### Ray‑Triangle Intersection (GPU‑friendly)

```hlsl
// HLSL 5.0 shader snippet (DXR)
RWTriangleBVH bvh : register(t0);
[[maxthreaddepth(64,1,1)]] void RayTrace(uint3 DTID : SV_DispatchThreadID)
{
    float3 rayDir = Normalize(RayDirection);
    IntersectData hit = bvh.Intersect(RayOrigin, rayDir);
    if (hit.valid) {
        float3 worldPos = hit.position;
        // write to RWStructuredBuffer for later shading
        OutputHit[hit.id] = hit;
    }
}
```
*This pattern uses a bounding‑volume hierarchy (BVH) node traversal; the BVH is built offline (CPU‑side) with `BvhBuilder` from Intel’s Embree (2024‑02) <https://www.embree.org/> and uploaded to a `RWByteAddressBuffer`.*

