## 4. Collision Detection & Narrow‑Phase Queries  

| Test | Core mathematics | Typical engine call | Performance class | When to prefer |
|------|------------------|----------------------|-------------------|----------------|
| **Capsule ↔ Capsule** | Reduce each capsule to its axis and radius; compute distance between two line segments (Segment ↔ Segment) using the *closest‑point* formulation. | `PhysX::CollisionTest::capsuleCapsule`, Unity `Physics.CheckSphere` with offset | O(1) | Typical character‑character collisions; tolerant to small penetration. |
| **Sphere ↔ Plane** | `signedDist = Dot(N, P) + D` where `N` is plane normal; if `|signedDist| < radius` → collision. | `Unreal Engine KismetMathLibrary::PlaneProject` + radius test | O(1) | Ground checks, bouncing, slopes. |
| **Convex Hull ↔ Convex Hull** | Separating Axis Theorem (SAT) on edge normals of both hulls; iterate over ~`O(n)` axes but early‑out on first separating axis. | Bullet `convexConvexCollision`, PhysX `ConvexCollisionDesc` | O(n) worst‑case, usually < 8 axes | Fast for debris, projectiles, enemy hit‑boxes when objects are convex‑decomposed. |
| **Ray ↔ Compound (multiple shapes)** | Combine per‑shape A
